course: dictionary
lesson: 13811
title: Irredeemable: beyond saving
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Irredeemable means so bad that it cannot be saved, fixed or made better. Look at the word in parts: the start «ir-» means not, and «redeemable» means able to be saved or made right again. Put together, irredeemable means not able to be saved.
explain: «The villain in the story was irredeemable, with not one kind act to his name.» The clue is «not one kind act». Even a bad character can sometimes change, but this one never does, so he cannot be made better. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: The word also has a money meaning. «The old shop voucher was irredeemable, so it could not be swapped back for cash.» Here it means the voucher cannot be exchanged for money. The context tells you which meaning is right, so always read the words around the word.
fact: Irredeemable means so bad that it cannot be saved, fixed or made better.
fact: «Irredeemable» can also describe a voucher or bond that cannot be swapped back for money.
fact: The start «ir-» means not, so the word is built from «not» and «redeemable».
fact: Many people believe no person is truly irredeemable, because people can change for the better.
fact: «Irredeemably» is the adverb: «The sweater was irredeemably torn.» It means in a way that cannot be fixed.
exercise: «The villain in the story was irredeemable, with not one kind act to his name.» What does irredeemable mean? | *So bad that he cannot be saved or made better | Lost in the forest | Very tired and hungry | Happy to help others
exercise: «The old sweater was an irredeemable mess, full of holes.» What does irredeemable suggest? | *Too badly damaged to be fixed | Very warm and soft | Bright yellow | Brand new and clean
exercise: Priya says her shop voucher is irredeemable. What does this mean for money? | It is worth twice as much as cash | It must be spent on Monday | *It cannot be swapped back for cash
test: Many people say no person is truly irredeemable. What does this mean? | Some people are always lost | Only villains are kind | *Nobody is so bad that they cannot change for the better | Everybody is rich
test: Which word is closest in meaning to irredeemable? | Tiny | *Hopeless | Cheerful | Sleepy
exam: What can you do with an irredeemable voucher? | Post it to a friend for a refund | Use it to buy any toy | Swap it back for cash | *Nothing, because it cannot be swapped back for money
